  <h1>About</h1>
  <p class="todo">TODO: headshot and one candid working photo.</p>

  <p class="lede">I'm Ari. I run marketing for a dispensary in Grass Valley, California, and I write code when the thing I want doesn't exist yet.</p>

  <p>Half my life in Israel, half in America. Photoshop at eleven, Visual Basic at twelve, a C++ book after one day at my mom's office at GE. Nobody paid me for any of it until I was eighteen. Two cultures and a lot of travel left me with one rule for work: design has to speak the language of the people it's for.</p>

  <p>One startup behind me. Three years building a product for Shopify stores, raised money, signed clients, didn't close the second round. It taught me I can build anything I set my mind to.</p>

  <p>The dispensary job started as a conversation with the owners before the doors opened. Ten hours the first week, full time since the second month. A large share of our budget goes to local nonprofits and I'm the one handing over the checks, plus a website or a logo or an event when they need one. That's the part of the job I like most.</p>

  <p>Off the clock: chess (around 1500 to 1600, blitz with a drink), the Bucks (followed Giannis from draft night to the trade, fear the deer), mechanical watches (a Speedmaster is next), and markets. I'm a value investor who gets as excited about bond yields as about a stock surging, but new technology is the most fun to invest in. Evaluating something new is where my product designer chops get tested.</p>
</Base>
